---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Brighter Sites"
  description="Learn how Brighter Sites handles information from its marketing website, client portal, communications, and project workflow."
>
  <section class="page-intro legal-intro">
    <div class="container legal-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        This policy explains what information Brighter Sites handles, why we use
        it, and the choices available to you when you visit our website, contact
        us, or use the Brighter Sites client portal.
      </p>
      <div class="legal-version-note" role="note">
        <strong>Version 1.1</strong>
        <span>Effective September 2, 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section legal-section">
    <div class="container legal-shell legal-copy">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy applies to the Brighter Sites marketing website at
          brightersites.app, the Brighter Sites client portal, and related
          communications and project workflows operated by Brighter Sites. It does
          not control the privacy practices of unrelated websites or services that
          we may link to.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information you provide</h2>
        <p>
          You may provide information when you email Brighter Sites, create or use
          a client-portal account, complete project intake, review project
          materials, acknowledge agreements, approve launch, or otherwise work
          with us. Depending on the interaction, this may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>name, email address, business or practice name, and contact details;</li>
          <li>project goals, requested pages, services, locations, branding preferences, public contact information, credentials, biographies, and website content;</li>
          <li>files, images, written materials, approvals, questions, and other project communications; and</li>
          <li>signer name and other information used to document contract acknowledgment or launch approval.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Portal, security, and acceptance records</h2>
        <p>
          The client portal uses authenticated accounts and project membership to
          limit access to the appropriate project. To support account security,
          project administration, and reliable records, Brighter Sites and its
          service providers may process account identifiers, authenticated email
          addresses, timestamps, request metadata, and similar technical records.
        </p>
        <p>
          When a client electronically acknowledges a project document or gives a
          recorded approval, Brighter Sites may retain the accepted document or
          content, document title and version, content hash, acceptance wording,
          signer name, authenticated email address, timestamp, IP address,
          user-agent information, project identifier, and audit identifier. These
          records help show what was presented and accepted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Marketing website and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites uses a first-party Website Intelligence analytics
          tracker on the marketing site to understand how visitors use the site
          and to improve pages, navigation, and services. Depending on the
          interaction, the tracker may record page views, entry status, referring
          website hostname, broad device category, and selected interactions such
          as contact, email, phone, service, appointment, client-portal, or
          outbound-link clicks.
        </p>
        <p>
          The tracker uses randomly generated identifiers stored in browser
          sessionStorage and localStorage to distinguish sessions and recognize
          returning visitors for up to 180 days. The tracker does not use cookies.
          It respects supported browser privacy signals such as Global Privacy
          Control and Do Not Track. Analytics requests are sent to the Brighter
          Sites first-party analytics service. Brighter Sites does not use this
          analytics system for cross-site behavioral advertising.
        </p>
        <p>
          Hosting, content-delivery, security, analytics, and network providers
          may process ordinary technical request information such as IP address,
          browser or device information, requested URL, and timestamps as part of
          delivering, measuring, and protecting the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. How we use information</h2>
        <p>Brighter Sites may use information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>respond to inquiries and communicate about potential or active projects;</li>
          <li>design, build, review, launch, maintain, and support websites and related services;</li>
          <li>operate and secure the client portal and other business systems;</li>
          <li>maintain project, approval, contract, billing, security, and audit records;</li>
          <li>troubleshoot problems, prevent misuse, and protect Brighter Sites, clients, and service providers;</li>
          <li>improve Brighter Sites services and internal workflows; and</li>
          <li>comply with legal, accounting, tax, insurance, or dispute-preservation obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Service providers and disclosure</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites uses service providers for functions such as hosting,
          content delivery, authentication, databases, source control, email,
          storage, security, and other business operations. Those providers may
          process information as needed to provide their services to Brighter
          Sites and are subject to their own terms and privacy practices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites may also disclose information when reasonably necessary
          to comply with law or legal process, protect rights or security, address
          fraud or misuse, complete a business transfer, or work with professional
          advisers who have an appropriate need for the information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. No sale of personal information</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites does not sell personal information to advertisers and
          does not use client-portal or project information to build cross-site
          advertising profiles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Sensitive and regulated information</h2>
        <p>
          Do not send passwords, recovery codes, payment-card details, Social
          Security numbers, protected health information (PHI), medical details,
          or other highly sensitive or regulated information through ordinary
          email, the marketing website, or the project portal unless Brighter
          Sites has expressly accepted that type of information under a separate
          compliant scope and any required agreement is already in place.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites keeps information for as long as reasonably necessary for
          the purpose for which it was collected, to provide and document the
          services, maintain security and business records, satisfy legal or
          accounting obligations, preserve accepted agreements and approvals, and
          resolve disputes. Retention periods may differ by record type. When
          information is no longer reasonably needed, Brighter Sites may delete,
          de-identify, or securely archive it as appropriate.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Security</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites uses reasonable administrative and technical safeguards
          appropriate to its services. No website, network, storage system, or
          transmission method can be guaranteed completely secure, and Brighter
          Sites cannot promise that an incident or unauthorized access will never
          occur.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Your choices and requests</h2>
        <p>
          You may contact Brighter Sites to ask a privacy question or request
          access, correction, or deletion of information associated with you.
          Whether a particular request can or must be fulfilled may depend on the
          type of record, an active project or contract, security needs, legal
          obligations, and the law that applies to the request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>12. Children</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites provides business website services and does not direct
          its website or client portal to children. Do not submit information
          about a child through Brighter Sites systems unless it is necessary for
          an agreed business purpose and lawful to provide it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites may update this Privacy Policy as its services, systems,
          or legal obligations change. The current version and effective or
          revision date will be posted on this page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions may be sent to
          <a href="mailto:help@brightersites.app">help@brightersites.app</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 54rem;
  }

  .legal-intro h1 {
    max-width: 13ch;
  }

  .legal-version-note {
    display: inline-grid;
    gap: .2rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: .9rem 1.05rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--teal);
    background: var(--teal-light);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-version-note strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal-section {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .legal-copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.2rem;
  }

  .legal-copy section {
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-copy section:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .legal-copy h2 {
    margin-bottom: .8rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 1.8rem);
  }

  .legal-copy p,
  .legal-copy li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal-copy p + p,
  .legal-copy p + ul,
  .legal-copy ul + p {
    margin-top: .85rem;
  }

  .legal-copy ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: .55rem;
    margin: .85rem 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-copy a {
    color: var(--teal-dark);
    font-weight: 750;
  }
</style>
